\begin{historical}
The sea of nodes was introduced by Cliff Click in his 1995 PhD thesis~\cite{click1995}, building on earlier work on value graphs and global code motion. The approach was adopted by the Java HotSpot compiler (C2) and later by Graal and V8 TurboFan. The sea of nodes' ability to unify data and control flow in a single graph, and to support aggressive global optimizations, has made it the preferred IR for high-performance just-in-time compilers.
\end{historical}

